From a7e9d558ca5ea68d3b1ed6225a173723453d51e7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 06:23:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] plugin *_nowait probes never wait on a sweep another
 thread holds

A force reload (hermes-sync mods-reload) unloads first, so `_discovered` is
False while the sweep thread holds `_discovery_lock`. `_nowait_plugin_set`
then fell through to a blocking `discover_plugins()`, which parked the
gateway event loop 36 s on laptop-1 (kanban_run -> build_kanban_policy ->
_resolve_toolsets -> _get_platform_tools -> get_plugin_toolset_keys_nowait)
and timed out Desktop's backend connects.

The probe now tries the lock non-blocking. Free and discovered: live set,
remembered per manager. Busy (another thread's sweep or a background scan):
the last live set, else last launch's persisted set, else on the event loop
an empty set (never block there). Blocking stays only for an idle,
never-discovered manager, or off the loop when nothing is known. A retry
after a failed sweep runs inline only off the loop.

Every async caller (session_policy, toolset_validation, enabled_mcp_server_names,
banner) goes through this one helper; hook_unused_nowait was already
non-blocking.

